01:12:50,120 --> 01:12:55,280
fully assembled personal computer with color graphics.

687
01:12:55,280 --> 01:12:59,680
It was a huge success, making Apple a serious player

688
01:12:59,680 --> 01:13:02,270
in the tech industry.

689
01:13:02,270 --> 01:13:06,660
But success didn't come without challenges.

690
01:13:06,660 --> 01:13:09,420
The computer market was competitive

691
01:13:09,420 --> 01:13:13,480
and Apple needed to innovate constantly.

692
01:13:13,480 --> 01:13:17,740
Jobs obsession with perfection sometimes caused conflicts

693
01:13:17,740 --> 01:13:20,220
with employees and investors,

694
01:13:20,220 --> 01:13:23,300
but it also drove the company to create products

695
01:13:23,300 --> 01:13:27,720
that were revolutionary, not just functional.

696
01:13:27,720 --> 01:13:32,590
The 1980s brought both triumph and turmoil.

697
01:13:32,590 --> 01:13:36,230
Apple launched the Macintosh in 1984,

698
01:13:36,230 --> 01:13:40,310
introducing a graphical user interface and a mouse,

699
01:13:40,310 --> 01:13:43,050
innovations that made computing accessible

700
01:13:43,050 --> 01:13:47,870
to ordinary people, not just tech experts.

701
01:13:47,870 --> 01:13:56,270
The launch was historic with the famous 1984 commercial directed by Ridley Scott, which

702
01:13:56,270 --> 01:13:59,600
aired during the Super Bowl.

703
01:13:59,600 --> 01:14:07,520
It portrayed Apple as a rebel against conformity, symbolizing innovation and creativity.

704
01:14:07,520 --> 01:14:16,230
However, internal conflicts led to Steve Jobs leaving Apple in 1985.

705
01:14:16,230 --> 01:14:23,740
Many thought this was the end of the visionary leader, but Jobs' journey was far from over.

706
01:14:23,740 --> 01:14:30,380
During his time away from Apple, Jobs founded Next, a computer company focused on high-end

707
01:14:30,380 --> 01:14:34,540
machines for education and business.

708
01:14:34,540 --> 01:14:41,740
He also acquired Pixar, turning it into the most successful animation studio in history,

709
01:14:41,740 --> 01:14:45,410
producing hits like Toy Story.

710
01:14:45,410 --> 01:14:53,070
These experiences taught Jobs important lessons about business, technology, storytelling, and

711
01:14:53,070 --> 01:14:57,950
leadership, which he would later bring back to Apple.

712
01:14:57,950 --> 01:15:02,730
In 1997, Apple was struggling.

713
01:15:02,730 --> 01:15:10,110
The company was near bankruptcy, losing millions, and products weren't selling.

714
01:15:10,110 --> 01:15:13,740
That's when Steve Jobs returned.

715
01:15:13,740 --> 01:15:23,130
He brought a clear vision, Apple must focus on innovation, simplicity, and design excellence.

716
01:15:23,130 --> 01:15:30,630
Jobs made bold moves, he cut unnecessary products, streamlined the product line, and focused

717
01:15:30,630 --> 01:15:34,840
on creating devices that people loved.

718
01:15:34,840 --> 01:15:41,550
His philosophy was simple, design is not just what it looks like.

719
01:15:41,550 --> 01:15:44,340
Design is how it works.

720
01:15:44,340 --> 01:15:46,420
The result?

721
01:15:46,420 --> 01:15:53,310
The iMac, introduced in 1998, became an instant hit.

722
01:15:53,310 --> 01:16:01,110
Its colorful design, easy to use interface, and unique look made Apple cool again.

723
01:16:01,110 --> 01:16:04,500
But Jobs didn't stop there.

724
01:16:04,500 --> 01:16:11,580
He revolutionized music with the iPod and iTunes, smartphones with the iPhone, tablets

725
01:16:11,580 --> 01:16:17,340
with the iPad, and smartwatches with the Apple Watch.

726
01:16:17,340 --> 01:16:24,220
Each product wasn't just a device, it was a statement about innovation, simplicity,

727
01:16:24,220 --> 01:16:26,830
and lifestyle.

728
01:16:26,830 --> 01:16:34,100
Apple's strategies for becoming a global tech leader can be summarized in key lessons.

729
01:16:34,100 --> 01:16:41,860
Think differently, Apple didn't just make products, it created experiences.

730
01:16:41,860 --> 01:16:50,700
and simplicity, jobs cut unnecessary complexity to create intuitive products.

731
01:16:50,700 --> 01:16:57,730
Innovation through design, every detail mattered, from hardware to software.

732
01:16:57,730 --> 01:17:07,520
Build an ecosystem, iTunes, iCloud, App Store, and devices all connected seamlessly.

733
01:17:07,520 --> 01:17:15,860
And loyalty, Apple customers weren't just buyers, they became lifelong fans.

734
01:17:15,860 --> 01:17:20,310
Jobs also taught the importance of resilience.

735
01:17:20,310 --> 01:17:28,090
He was fired, faced bankruptcy, and endured failures, yet he returned stronger, showing

736
01:17:28,090 --> 01:17:32,790
that setbacks are stepping stones to success.

737
01:17:32,790 --> 01:17:41,430
Today, Apple is worth over $3 trillion, employs millions worldwide, and its products have shaped

738
01:17:41,430 --> 01:17:46,630
the way billions of people communicate, work, and entertain themselves.

739
01:17:48,060 --> 01:17:53,900
From a small garage project to the most valuable technology company in history,

740
01:17:53,900 --> 01:17:59,660
Apple's story is a testament to vision, persistence, and relentless innovation.

741
01:17:59,660 --> 01:18:08,330
The story of Apple teaches us that success is not just about ideas, it's about execution,

742
01:18:08,330 --> 01:18:14,890
design, persistence, and the courage to challenge the status quo.

743
01:18:14,890 --> 01:18:22,110
If you work hard, stay focused, and never stop innovating, even a small idea can become

744
01:18:22,110 --> 01:18:25,400
a global revolution.

745
01:18:25,400 --> 01:18:31,470
Apple didn't just make computers and phones, it changed the world.

746
01:18:31,470 --> 01:18:40,180
This story is more than business history, it's a lesson in creativity, vision, and determination.

747
01:18:40,180 --> 01:18:47,060
Steve Jobs' life proves that with passion, boldness, and persistence, you can overcome

748
01:18:47,060 --> 01:18:51,480
any challenge and build something legendary.

749
01:18:51,480 --> 01:18:58,200
From a garage in California to a trillion-dollar empire, Apple's story shows that innovation

750
01:18:58,200 --> 01:19:01,640
and dedication can turn dreams into reality.
